# Failure-boundary discipline
Follow the complete reported call sequence. A constructor, insertion, or setup call is not automatically
where a later serialization, save, iteration, or access failure is observed. Choose the supplied public
operation whose execution exposes the reported failure; request the relevant caller/callee when that
boundary is not visible. Do not choose a nearby function merely because its name occurs in the issue.
When the host says this is the final decision round, select only from evidence already returned or explicitly
request missing context and accept an abstention. Never invent source or location IDs to avoid abstention.
Keep any requested rationale short (one or two sentences); emit the structured response when the decision is made.

